    "created_at": "2024-10-23T04:31:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-10-23T04:31:41Z",
    "body": "Well, the question is whether we need an example for every piece of standard text. Usually we add them to illustrate particularly important or confusing points. I think the fact that boolean attribute values are ASCII case-insensitive is not one of those points, especially since almost everything in HTML is ASCII case-insensitive. For example, we don't have an example for how tag names are ASCII case-insensitive, or attribute names, or boolean attribute names...",
