    "created_at": "2024-10-23T06:02:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-10-23T06:02:50Z",
    "body": "I agree that we don't need to illustrate all case-insensitive cases.\r\n\r\nHowever, in this particular case, we are illustrating the value of an attribute, which is case-sensitive in at least many cases, e.g., `title`. And the case sensitivity of `accesskey` seems to also have caused some inconformity in the past: #4799 \r\n\r\nBut this is a rather small change. I would defer to you for the best judgment since you have a better understanding of the standard :+1: ",
